HST PDF: toolbar for every window width, fit width, previous/next page, rotate, save a copy, ≡ menu.

Audit 13/11 (HST PDF): at 1100 px the "Sign" button was cut at the right edge, and the viewer had
no buttons for fit width, previous/next page, rotate or save a copy, and no way to help.

- Narrow window (PdfViewerWindow::Resize -> fitToolbar): the toolbar takes the widest of six
  levels that fits. The search box shrinks first (24, 16, 10 characters), then Open, Print,
  Save a Copy, Fit Page and Fit Width show only their icon (their label stays the accessible
  name), then "Page" is hidden, then the search box goes to 6 characters. "Edit in HST Draw" and
  "Sign" never change. HSTPdfInfo reports ToolbarLevel.
- New buttons (Vietnamese tooltips with the shortcut, like the others): Save a Copy (Ctrl+Shift+S;
  the open file's bytes unchanged, to a new file chosen in the save dialog; the open file itself is
  refused), Fit Width (Ctrl+2; the zoom box item reads "Vừa bề rộng" too), Rotate (Ctrl+R; the view
  turns 90° clockwise), Previous page (Ctrl+Page Up), Next page (Ctrl+Page Down), and a ≡ menu
  button at the right end with the commands of the office ribbon's ≡ menu: HST Office Help
  (.uno:HelpIndex), Report a Problem to HASON TECH (org.hst.office.vi:ReportError), About HST
  Office (.uno:About). Fit Page gets an icon so it can drop its label.
- Rotation is a view setting (PdfPageView::setRotation, pages and thumbnails, back to upright for
  each opened document): the page is rendered at the swapped size and turned (Bitmap::Rotate), and
  toPagePoint/toPixel map between the turned view and the upright page, so text selection, search
  highlights and the signature box keep their page points and signing is unchanged.
- Commands for the runtime checks: .uno:HSTPdfRotate (Rotation in degrees, else +90),
  .uno:HSTPdfPreviousPage, .uno:HSTPdfNextPage, .uno:HSTPdfSaveCopy (TargetURL); HSTPdfInfo
  reports Rotation and the new controls in ToolbarLayout.

License: the modified files keep their license (MPL-2.0).
